    "end": "They'd opened everything. Even Nan's.",
    "caption": "The sherry was a trap too.\n\nCrumb: 5.2 million people, a 24-hour day, one moon, and one rule on Christmas Eve: whoever eats the mince pie left out for Santa becomes Santa until morning. Every chimney on the planet, in whatever they had on. Most dads find out around eleven, with crumbs down their jumper.\n\nI spent a Christmas Eve with a family there. I tidied up the plate before bed, to be helpful. I did the whole southern hemisphere.\n\n(The story goes that British children leave Father Christmas a mince pie and a glass of sherry, and a carrot for the reindeer. On Crumb, the carrot's the only safe thing on the plate.)\n\nWhat would your kids open first?"
  },
  "first_comment": "Nan's was a foot spa. The kids have been taking turns in it all morning.",
